35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The billing is area-based, not headcount. We pay for empty desks. Moving them costs 6,200 yen each.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found the printer row is nine decibels louder, and my chair takes days to adjust. Please, let’s not put me there.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, the badge records are brutal. Early birds claim seats before half of us even arrive.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, exactly. First-come is a rigged game. We need a rule that ignores arrival time entirely.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, I found that sitting close meant we stopped writing notes because we could just ask. Proximity actually saves us time.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, the 6,200 yen per desk charge means every future change is expensive. We must pick a layout that won't need constant shuffling.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I understand the cost. But if I sit by the printer, my body will hurt for days. Please, let’s keep the quiet spots for us.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, four to nine minutes daily is a huge drain. Plus, the arrival gap means first-come is already broken.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, that confirms it. Proximity is a resource, not a luxury. We need to design for it, not leave it to chance.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, I also found the new joiners learned by overhearing. If we sit apart, we lose that quiet learning.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, I agree. The 6,200 yen penalty makes frequent changes financially impossible. We need a stable structure that respects the area-based billing reality.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I understand the cost. But the physio said my chair takes days to settle. If I move often, my body will never be comfortable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Victoria, stability is good, but four to nine minutes daily is a massive drain. I need a layout that minimizes that setup time.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, stability is the only way to protect your comfort. Frequent moves would destroy the setup you need.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, I agree. If we sit apart, we lose that quiet learning. We need to keep people close enough to talk.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@May, stability is key. If we pick a fixed layout, we avoid the 6,200 yen penalty and the daily setup drain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, thank you. If I stay in one spot, my chair can finally settle. I really hope we can keep the quiet window side for me.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"@Victoria, I agree. Fixed desks mean I plug in once and work. No daily scramble. That saves my gaps.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, stability is the only way to protect your comfort. Frequent moves would destroy the setup you need.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, I agree. Fixed desks protect the quiet learning we need. I’m relieved we’re choosing stability over chance.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
